 When a ceiling is reached TA stops the agent, prints which ceiling and what was used, records the outcome `aborted_budget` on the goal, and builds the draft from the partial work, marked as incomplete (`ta draft view` says so first). What it can promise: TA reads the runtime's usage report after each agent turn, so the agent is stopped at the first turn boundary after the ceiling is crossed. Overshoot is possible by up to one turn (a single long turn can cost a lot); undershoot is capped, since a goal is never stopped before it reaches the ceiling. Ceilings are enforced only for headless runs, because that is where TA reads the usage report. `--max-usd` needs a price: from the runtime's reported cost or the price table. For an unpriced model it warns and only `--max-tokens` applies. A goal that finishes on its own over the ceiling is not marked incomplete.
 
+### Spend across goals and interactive sessions
+
+`ta cost report` answers "where is the money going" across TA goals and the long interactive sessions TA does not launch. Each source is optional and auto-detected:
+
+- TA goals: this project's goal records
+- Claude Code sessions: `~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl`
+- OMP sessions: `~/.omp/agent/sessions/**/*.jsonl`
+
+```bash
+ta cost report                                   # grouped by source
+ta cost report --since 2026-10-01 --group-by day
+ta cost report --group-by source,model --project myapp
+ta cost report --group-by context_bucket         # cost by prompt size
+ta cost report --group-by origin_class           # goals only: asked / suggested / unasked
+ta cost report --json                            # machine-readable
+```
+
+`--since` and `--until` take a date or an RFC 3339 time. `--group-by` takes a comma-separated list of `day`, `source`, `model`, `project`, `context_bucket`, `origin_class`. `--project` matches a project name by case-insensitive substring.
+
+Example output:
+
+```
+Sources:
+  ta_goal      12 goal(s) in /work/app/.ta/goals
+  claude_code  3 file(s), 2832 row(s) read, 1267 counted, 1565 duplicate(s) dropped, 0 synthetic skipped, 0 unreadable (/home/me/.claude/projects)
+  omp          not found (/home/me/.omp/agent/sessions); skipped
+
+source                                turns  goals         input        output      cache read   cache write   cost USD
+claude_code                           1,267      0         3,100       990,000     603,000,000    14,600,000     283.42 ~
+ta_goal                                   0     12       410,000     2,100,000      90,000,000     6,000,000      41.10 ~
+TOTAL                                 1,267     12       413,100     3,090,000     693,000,000    20,600,000     324.52
+
+Context size per turn:
+source       context        turns       cache read   cost USD
+claude_code  0-50k            140       3,100,000       2.90
+claude_code  >400k            610     420,000,000     181.00
+```
+
+How the numbers are made:
+
+- **Deduplicated.** Claude Code writes one message as several transcript rows with the same message id. Each id is counted once (the last row wins), and `<synthetic>` placeholder rows are skipped. The header says how many rows were dropped.
+- **Exact or estimated.** A cost is exact when its source reported it (OMP, or a goal whose runtime reported the cost). Otherwise it is estimated from the price table and marked `~`. A model with no price row is counted in tokens with a cost of 0; TA never invents a price. Put real rates in `.ta/pricing.toml`.
+- **Cache writes.** When a transcript splits cache writes, the 1 hour class is priced at 2x the input rate and the 5 minute class at 1.25x. In `.ta/pricing.toml` a row may add `cache_write_1h` (USD per million tokens) to change the 1 hour rate.
+- **Context size.** Each turn is placed in a bucket by the size of its prompt (fresh input plus cache read plus cache write): 0-50k, 50-100k, 100-200k, 200-400k, over 400k. Long sessions that sit in the top buckets are where cache-read cost piles up.
+- **Missing sources** are listed as skipped, not as errors. With `--since` or `--until`, rows that carry no timestamp are left out and counted in a note.
+
